Basic Workflow for Visualize
****************************

The basic workflow this package requires the user to open a port for
communication between Macaulay2 and the web browser. Once the port is open, the
*note visualize: visualize, method can be used freely. In particular, the
workflow is as follows:

  * 1. Load or install the package.
  * 2. Open a port with *note openPort: openPort, method for communication with
    the browser. It is up to the user to choose port and also to close the port
    when finished.
  * 3. Define an object you wish to visualize. For example, a graph, poset,
    digraph, etc.
  * 4. Run the *note visualize: visualize, method. This will open the browser
    with an interactive interface. This session is in communication with
    Macaulay2 through the open port above. At this point you can edit and
    manipulate the created object.
  * 5. End the session and export work back to Macaulay2.
  * 6. Continue manipulating the object and repeat steps 3-5 as necessary.
  * 7. When finished, close the port with *note closePort: closePort, or
    restart Macaulay2.

